 //! (texelFetch samples at the texel's centre), and GL's bottom-up rows (the
 //! vertex stage flips Y so that memory layout matches SWGL's exactly).
+//!
+//! The same translation also writes GLSL ES 1.0 (`essl`), for OpenGL ES 2
+//! GPUs that lack vertex texture fetch, such as the PowerVR SGX in iOS
+//! devices of the A4-A6 generation. Their limits are much like 9_3's; the
+//! differences are spelling, and that GL's rows need no flipping.
 
